     1	# Script Module Loading Fix - Context
     2	
     3	## What we're doing
     4	
     5	Fixing a race condition where Livewire v4 SFC/MFC script modules (containing `Alpine.data()` registrations) load asynchronously but Alpine processes `x-data` synchronously, causing "Can't find variable" errors.
     6	
     7	Discussions: #9591, #9737, #9830
     8	
     9	## Key files
    10	
    11	- `js/features/supportJsModules.js` - JS-side module loading (effect hook, async import, pending asset tracking)
    12	- `js/lifecycle.js` - Livewire/Alpine boot process, `interceptInit` callback, `Alpine.start()`
    13	- `js/component.js` - Component constructor, `processEffects()`
    14	- `js/store.js` - `initComponent()`, component registry
    15	- `js/$wire.js` - Existing `$js` pending asset handling (lines 165-193)
    16	- `js/features/supportMorphDom.js` - Morph trigger via `interceptMessage` + `onMorph`
    17	- `js/features/supportScriptsAndAssets.js` - How `@script`/`@endscript` works (synchronous, no race condition)
    18	- `js/morph.js` - DOM morphing implementation
    19	- `js/request/index.js` - Request lifecycle (lines 404-458: success handler, hook ordering)
    20	- `js/request/message.js` - Message lifecycle hooks (`invokeOnMorph` uses `Promise.all`)
 succeeded in 51ms:
     1	# Script Module Loading: Race Condition Analysis and Solution Ideas
     2	
     3	## The Problem
     4	
     5	Livewire v4 SFC/MFC components can have co-located JavaScript files (either `<script>` blocks in SFCs or separate `.js` files in MFCs). These are compiled into ES modules served from `/livewire/js/{component}.js` and loaded dynamically via `import()`.
     6	
     7	The core issue: **script modules load asynchronously, but Alpine processes `x-data` synchronously**. When a script module contains `Alpine.data()` registrations, those registrations aren't available when Alpine evaluates `x-data="componentName"`, causing "Can't find variable" errors.
     8	
     9	**Reported in:**
    10	- [#9591](https://github.com/livewire/livewire/discussions/9591) - SFC with `Alpine.data()` in `<script>` block
    11	- [#9737](https://github.com/livewire/livewire/discussions/9737) - Same issue, also affects MFC `.js` files
    12	- [#9830](https://github.com/livewire/livewire/discussions/9830) - Detailed analysis of MFC `.js` files not working with `Alpine.data()`
    13	
    14	## Current Architecture
    15	
    16	### How script modules are served
    17	
    18	1. The compiler (`Parser.php`) injects a `scriptModuleSrc()` method into the component class, pointing to the compiled `.js` file
    19	2. `SupportJsModules.php` adds a `scriptModule` effect (a hash of the file's mtime) during `dehydrate()`
    20	3. A route at `/livewire/js/{encoded-name}.js` serves the file contents

